# ToDo-AI Project Rules for IDE Assistance

## Code Style
- Use Spring Boot best practices
- Follow Java naming conventions (camelCase for methods/variables, PascalCase for classes)
- Maximum line length: 120 characters
- Always use dependency injection with @RequiredArgsConstructor (Lombok)
- Add JavaDoc comments for public methods

## Architecture Guidelines
- Controllers: Handle HTTP requests, delegate to service
- Services: Contain business logic, use repositories for data access
- Repositories: Use Spring Data JPA, minimal custom logic
- Models: JPA entities with proper annotations
- DTOs: For API request/response data transfer

## REST API Conventions
- Base path: `/api`
- Version prefix: `v1`, `v2`, etc.
- HTTP Methods: GET (read), POST (create), PUT (update), DELETE (delete)
- Status codes: 200 (OK), 201 (Created), 204 (No Content), 400 (Bad Request), 404 (Not Found), 500 (Server Error)
- Response format: JSON with camelCase keys

## Spring Boot Configuration
- Use application.properties for configuration
- Environment-specific profiles: application-dev.properties, application-prod.properties
- Enable validation with @Valid on request DTOs
- Use @Transactional for service layer methods that modify data

## Testing Conventions
- Test classes: Use @SpringBootTest for integration tests
- Unit tests: Use Mockito for mocking dependencies
- Test naming: testDescribeWhat_ThenExpectWhat()

## Important Files
- pom.xml: Dependency management
- application.properties: Configuration
- .claude: Project context for Claude
- README.md: Project documentation

## Common Commands
- Build: `mvn clean install`
- Run: `mvn spring-boot:run`
- Test: `mvn test`
- Package: `mvn package`

